From 7b9d313ad80185185cde52b809e3331c55d221e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:39:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] WAN status: Connected follows the internet check; IPv6
 re-solicited after an outage (102.8 line)

- The header and the dashboard said Connected whenever a line held a lease. A line now counts as
  up while it holds a lease and the router's own internet check passes on it; IPv6 counts as up
  only while it has a default route.
- wanduck: native IPv6 never came back after an upstream outage. Once per outage, when the line is
  up again and IPv6 has no default route, the DHCPv6 client is restarted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/wanduck.c            | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++
 release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp | 79 ++++++++++++++--------
 release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp    | 52 ++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 161 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/wanduck.c b/release/src/router/rc/wanduck.c
index 49431bff11..ad7b19f636 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/wanduck.c
